{"authored" [{"question" "q-339239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The population $P(t)$ of fish in a pond after $t$ weeks can be modeled by the differential equation ${P}^{′}(t)=0.09P(t).$ If the fish population was $8\\,000$ after $18$ weeks, calculate the fish population after $23$ weeks. Round the final population to the nearest whole fish. Do not round intermediate values." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-339239/review.json" "file_sha256" "5d83849b4652926d691c79089bc22611ca970ef0ee0db0480be325bc8897c78a" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-339239/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "0de6276ad3ce980004a90e03931db22ca6409ee1075ec95d1190f98be213131b" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-339239/verification.json" "basis" 1694 "rationale" "The source lesson rounds the initial constant to three decimal places, then rounds the resulting later population to 12,547. That is its documented approximation method, confirmed by the revealed source solution. The study prompt now explicitly requires final-only nearest-whole rounding, whose mathematically correct value is 12,546. Preserve original source content and its 12,547 key in historical question content and immutable old answer fields; create new study field and answer identities with matching prompt, solution, choice and key."} {"question" "q-339239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The solution of $P'(t)=0.09P(t)$ satisfies\n\n$$P(t)=P(18)e^{0.09(t-18)}=8\\,000e^{0.09(t-18)}.$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$P(23)=8\\,000e^{0.45}\\approx12\\,546.49748392135.$$\n\nRounding only this final value to the nearest whole number gives approximately $12\\,546$ fish." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-339239/review.json" "file_sha256" "5d83849b4652926d691c79089bc22611ca970ef0ee0db0480be325bc8897c78a" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-339239/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "0de6276ad3ce980004a90e03931db22ca6409ee1075ec95d1190f98be213131b" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-339239/verification.json" "basis" 1694 "rationale" "The source lesson rounds the initial constant to three decimal places, then rounds the resulting later population to 12,547. That is its documented approximation method, confirmed by the revealed source solution. The study prompt now explicitly requires final-only nearest-whole rounding, whose mathematically correct value is 12,546. Preserve original source content and its 12,547 key in historical question content and immutable old answer fields; create new study field and answer identities with matching prompt, solution, choice and key."} {"question" "q-339239" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12\\,546"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-339239/review.json" "file_sha256" "5d83849b4652926d691c79089bc22611ca970ef0ee0db0480be325bc8897c78a" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-339239/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "0de6276ad3ce980004a90e03931db22ca6409ee1075ec95d1190f98be213131b" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-339239/verification.json" "basis" 1694 "rationale" "The source lesson rounds the initial constant to three decimal places, then rounds the resulting later population to 12,547. That is its documented approximation method, confirmed by the revealed source solution. The study prompt now explicitly requires final-only nearest-whole rounding, whose mathematically correct value is 12,546. Preserve original source content and its 12,547 key in historical question content and immutable old answer fields; create new study field and answer identities with matching prompt, solution, choice and key."} {"question" "q-339239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The population $P(t)$ of fish in a pond after $t$ weeks can be modeled by the differential equation ${P}^{′}(t)=0.09P(t).$ If the fish population was $8\\,000$ after $18$ weeks, calculate the fish population after $23$ weeks." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045453/state.json" "file_sha256" "99a5299203aeba32e76c6f786d7a5ba676f18e4a274b5636299dd4ac7ccdfec4" "basis" 1692 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045453/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-339239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The general solution to the given differential equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.09t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{0}$ is the initial fish population.\n\nWe are given that after $18$ weeks, the population was $8\\,000.$ So, substituting $t=18$ and $P(18)=8\\,000$ into our general solution and solving for ${P}_{0},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(18) & ={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.09\\cdot 18} \\\\ 8\\,000 & ={P}_{0}\\,{e}^{1.62} \\\\ {P}_{0} & =\\frac{8\\,000}{{e}^{1.62}} \\\\  & ≈1\\,583.190,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nHence, our particular solution is\n\n$$\nP(t)=1\\,583.190\\,{e}^{0.09t}.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the fish population after $23$ weeks. So, substituting $t=23$ into our particular solution, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(23) & =1\\,583.190\\,{e}^{0.09\\cdot 23} \\\\  & =1\\,583.190\\,{e}^{2.07} \\\\  & ≈12\\,547,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest whole number. \n\nTherefore, approximately $12\\,547$ fish will be in the pond after $23$ weeks." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045453/state.json" "file_sha256" "99a5299203aeba32e76c6f786d7a5ba676f18e4a274b5636299dd4ac7ccdfec4" "basis" 1692 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045453/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-339239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045453/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0cd27dca353e8df5d117d7b1c938d890f395fa761cd5532ea3e45a3180cf60a" "basis" 1692 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14045453/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [] "usage" {"q-339239" []} "basis" 1694 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186326271 17592186326272 17592186326273 17592186326274 17592186326275] "immutable_fields" [[17592186326270 :answer-field/correct] [17592186326270 :answer-field/id] [17592186326270 :answer-field/key] [17592186326270 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
